# The annotation model: ontos + bookmark membership + .yo: fragments:.
Annotations - fragments and ontos
description: how a user marks up a document - regions, and membership in ontologies
- >
  How a user marks up a document: **fragments** (regions of a node) and **onto membership**
  (filing a node or a fragment under an entity of an ontology - what used to be called tagging).
  Both live **on the target node** - they travel with the document, not in a side file. The
  user-facing flow is in [annotating](*::server:ui:annotating); companion chapters: the
  [logical graph](*::language:logical-graph) (omni), [metadata](*::meta) (`$defs`, `variant`),
  [pointers](*::language:pointers) (the `::` project scope, `*`/`&`), and
  [queries](*::language:pointers:queries).
- >
  There is no annotation *object* anymore: applying an onto is a plain **`&` bookmark** - a
  membership edge into the ontology - and everything an application used to say (a description,
  a parameter) lives on the **fragment**, which is an ordinary open node. This supersedes both
  earlier models: the per-file `/annotations/*.yo` applications, and the
  `yamlover-annotations` array element (both retired).
